# E2E

Playwright covers critical-path guest/host browser flows. Full setup and failure modes: **`e2e/README.md`**.

| Spec | Journey |
| ---- | ---- |
| `guest-claim-by-count.spec.ts` | Two phones tap the same receipt line at once; nobody ends up splitting |
| `guest-share-unit.spec.ts` | Sharing a Unit from the line's „⋯“ puts half on a friend right away |
| `guest-covered-seat.spec.ts` | One phone claims and pays for two seats; Host confirms both |
| `guest-pay-for-other-release.spec.ts` | A pay-for-others pick frees the covered Guest when the payer's phone leaves |
| `session-conflict.spec.ts` | Two browsers claim the same guest seat |
| `combined-guest-payment.spec.ts` | Host payment banner appears only after Revolut opens |
| `host-account-route.spec.ts` | Host Акаунт route: unsigned redirect; signed-in `/user-profile` and `/user-profile/security` |
| `host-onboarding.spec.ts` | Host replay hints; welcome dismiss |

## Prerequisites

- Dev Convex deployment with **`CLERK_JWT_ISSUER_DOMAIN`** set.
- **`.env.local`**: `VITE_CONVEX_URL`, `VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`, `CLERK_SECRET_KEY`; optional `E2E_CLERK_USER_EMAIL`.
- Terminal 1: `npx convex dev`; terminal 2: `pnpm run test:e2e` (or dev already on :3000).

Run E2E locally when you touch guest/host browser flows. CI runs only when `E2E_VITE_CONVEX_URL` is set.
